SUMMARY:Chasing Hilton Falls: A Summertime Hike
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/hilton-summer)**\n\n**Hilt
 on Falls is one of the best hiking spots close to Toronto\, and we’ll be
  heading there with the crew to take it all in!**\n\nThe route blends two 
 very different trail personalities into one amazing adventure. The Beaver 
 Dam Trail is wide and relaxed\, threading past active beaver ponds and alo
 ng the Niagara escarpment. If we’re lucky\, we may see some of these inc
 redible creatures at work.\n\nFrom there\, we move on to the Hilton Falls 
 Side Trail\, which becomes a more technical\, Bruce Trail singletrack with
  rocks and roots that make you pay attention to where you’re stepping\, 
 along with beautiful views from atop the escarpment.\n\nThe waterfall is t
 he centrepiece of this hike: a 10 metres fixture that flows over a rocky l
 edge into a pool flanked by the stone ruins of three 19th-century sawmills
 . It's one of the better pieces of trail-accessible industrial history any
 where close to the city.\n\nGood company\, good trails\, and an unforgetta
 ble day. See you there!\n\n**Highlights**\n**Hilton Falls:** A 10-metre dr
 op over the Escarpment edge\, framed by the stone ruins of three 19th-cent
 ury sawmills.\n**Beaver Ponds:** Active beaver ponds and wetlands along a 
 tributary of Sixteen Mile Creek. Move quietly and you might spot reptiles\
 , amphibians\, and a lot of beaver handiwork up close.\n**Close to the Cit
 y:** Our Trailhead sits less than an hour from downtown Toronto.\n\n**Even
 t cost: $50+HST (for explorer members) - $40 optional transport available.
 **\n**Register [here.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/hilton-s
 ummer)**\n\n**About Wilderness Union**\nWilderness Union is deliberate abo
 ut building an outdoors community that connects you to the life-changing m
 agic of the outdoors and helps you find your people.\n\nMembers range from
  20-40 years old. The group is a mix of GTA locals and newcomers to Toront
 o from within Canada and abroad.\n\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't ref
 lect our actual event attendance - we typically have 15-20 community membe
 rs at each event. Large enough that there's someone new to meet but small 
 enough that it's not overwhelming!\n\n***Learn more at our website [www.wi
 ldernessunion.com](https://www.wildernessunion.com/)***
